Q: Why doesn&#39;t color:inherit inside a ShadowRoot inherit the color from the root element? A: <h3><code>color</code> is an <em>inheritable style</em></h3>
<p>For all Inheritable styles that pierce shadowDOM see: <a href="https://htmlwithsuperpowers.netlify.app/styling/inheritable.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://htmlwithsuperpowers.netlify.app/styling/inheritable.html</a></p>
<p><code>:host</code> allows the Web Component (or your DIV with a shadowRoot)  <strong><em>user</em></strong> to <strong>override</strong> the <em>red</em> color.</p>
<p>If you want to control the color form <strong><em>inside</em></strong> the Web Component (or your DIV) then <strong>color the <code>span</code></strong></p>
<p>Note: using standard <em>Declarative ShadowDOM</em> to create the component:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;style&gt;
  my-web-component {
    font: 42px Arial;
    color: darkgreen;
    font-weight: bold;
    border-color: red;
  }
&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;my-web-component&gt;
  &lt;template shadowrootmode="open"&gt;
    &lt;style&gt;
    :host {
      color: red;
    }
    span {
      border: 3px dashed darkgreen;
      padding: .1em;
    }
    &lt;/style&gt;
    &lt;span&gt;
      Hello World
    &lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/template&gt;
&lt;/my-web-component&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: How to iterate the sequence of pulling array items from middle (eg:[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7] -&gt; 4 3 5 2 6 1 7 0) without generating the sequence number array? A: <p>You could take recursive generator approach by calling the function  with a depth first search and return later the values of left and right elements in reverse order.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function* getValues(array) {
    const
        right = array.pop(),
        hasLeft = !!array.length,
        left = array.shift(); 

    if (array.length) yield* getValues(array);
    yield right;
    if (hasLeft) yield left;
}

console.log(...getValues([0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7])); // 4 3 5 2 6 1 7 0
console.log(...getValues([0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6])); // 3 4 2 5 1 6 0</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>With an array of method strings.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function* getValues([...array], methods = ['pop', 'shift']) {
    if (!array.length) return;

    const
        method = methods.pop(),
        value = array[method]();

    yield* getValues(array, [method, ...methods]);
    yield value;
}

console.log(...getValues([0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7])); // 4 3 5 2 6 1 7 0
console.log(...getValues([0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6])); // 3 4 2 5 1 6 0</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: How to set height of actionbar tabs for android A: <p>By setting both the Application theme attribute android:actionBarSize and the ActionBar.TabView style attribute android:minHeight (or height) to 80 dp.
A basic example:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;style name="ThemeHoloWithActionBar" parent="android:Theme.Holo.Light"&gt;
    &lt;item name="android:actionBarTabStyle"&gt;@style/ActionBarTabStyle&lt;/item&gt;
    &lt;item name="android:actionBarSize"&gt;80dp&lt;/item&gt;
&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;style name="ActionBarTabStyle" parent="@android:style/Widget.Holo.ActionBar.TabView"&gt;
    &lt;item name="android:minHeight"&gt;80dp&lt;/item&gt;
&lt;/style&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Set theme in Manifest:</p>

<pre><code>   &lt;application
    android:icon="@drawable/ic_launcher"
    android:label="@string/app_name"
    android:theme="@style/ThemeHoloWithActionBar" &gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Activity</p>

<pre><code>        ActionBar actionbar = getActionBar();
        actionbar.setNavigationMode(ActionBar.NAVIGATION_MODE_TABS);
        actionbar.setDisplayShowTitleEnabled(false);
        actionbar.setDisplayShowHomeEnabled(false);
        ActionBar.Tab tabA = actionbar.newTab().setText("Tab A");
        ActionBar.Tab tabB = actionbar.newTab().setText("Tab B");
        ActionBar.Tab tabC = actionbar.newTab().setText("Tab C");
        tabA.setTabListener(new MyTabsListener());
        tabB.setTabListener(new MyTabsListener());
        tabC.setTabListener(new MyTabsListener());
        actionbar.addTab(tabA);
        actionbar.addTab(tabB);
        actionbar.addTab(tabC);
</code></pre>
